+                "Note: This is a neural architecture search task on a 7-node directed acyclic graph (DAG). "
+                "NASBench101-C uses 21 real-valued edge priorities, edge_0 through edge_20, "
+                "each in [0, 1], and an integer num_edges in [0, 9]. "
+                "The edge priorities follow upper-triangular row order: "
+                "(0,1), (0,2), ..., (0,6), (1,2), ..., (5,6). "
+                "The num_edges highest-priority entries are enabled; the values are priorities, "
+                "not binary adjacency entries. Equal priorities follow the implementation's sorting order. "
+                "The op_node_0 through op_node_4 parameters choose operations for nodes 1 through 5. "
+                "Node 0 is the input and node 6 is the output. "
+                "A graph without a connected input-to-output path is invalid and scores 0. "
+                "Specify all 21 edge priorities, num_edges, and all five op_node_* parameters "
+                "in every evaluation call."
+            )
         return (
             "Note: This is a neural architecture search task on a 7-node directed acyclic graph (DAG). "
             "The edge_* parameters form the upper-triangular adjacency matrix (0 or 1) of the DAG. "
